An almost complete distribution of Hack 1.0.2, including Part 2 (which is
missing from Google), has turned up at:

http://vmsone.com/~decuslib/unixsig/uni87a/hack/

The only problem with this distribution is that Part 8 is not the original. 
It's been repackaged, the files inside have the wrong name (shk.c instead
of hack.shk.c for example) and they have mail headers at the top.  The
files are in the same order, and so it's quite easy to fix by doing diff -w
against the Google version.  If these problems are fixed, and if WIZARD in
Part 1 is changed to the original definition of aeb, we have what appears
to be the original and complete Hack 1.0.2.

The other parts differ from the Google posts only in the Usenet headers,
where present, and in that the Google posts have some slight damage (some
of the indenting whitespace has been dropped).

